 "about": "SQL reserved words from public lists, for tools/osd-ddic-reserved.mjs. A system's dictionary refuses a table field named by a reserved word ('X is a reserved word (choose another field name)'); its own list is the dictionary table TRESE, which is system content and is never copied here. Each part names its public source. A word in any part is refused unless 'accepted' names it with the measurement that says a system takes it. 'allow' names a table field already in the tree, with its kind: system-has-it (a system's own table has the column), structure (not a database column), unmeasured (debt: measure on a system or rename). A new field is never added here to make the check pass; it is renamed.",
